---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Security"
  description="OpsRun security model: host keys, secrets, approvals, rollback, audit."
  path="/security"
>
  <p class="label">Trust model</p>
  <h1 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg">Security</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 max-w-[36rem] text-[15px] leading-6 text-fg-3">
    OpsRun runs powerful remote commands. Defaults prefer visibility and reversibility.
  </p>

  <ul class="mt-8 space-y-4 text-[15px] leading-6 text-fg-2">
    <li><strong class="text-fg">Validate first</strong> — parse and check before execute; use <code class="font-mono text-[12px]">--dry-run</code>.</li>
    <li><strong class="text-fg">Host keys</strong> — known_hosts verification is on by default.</li>
    <li><strong class="text-fg">Secrets</strong> — redacted in logs, TUI, and audit plaintext.</li>
    <li><strong class="text-fg">Audit</strong> — hash-chained JSONL; verify with <code class="font-mono text-[12px]">opsrun audit verify</code>.</li>
    <li><strong class="text-fg">Rollback</strong> — destructive steps without rollback are flagged.</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="note mt-8">
    Report vulnerabilities via
    <a href="https://github.com/Leo-Galli/opsrun/blob/main/SECURITY.md" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">SECURITY.md</a>.
    Do not open a public issue.
  </div>

  <p class="mt-4 text-[13px]">
    <a class="underline decoration-rule underline-offset-4" href="/docs/security">Full security docs</a>
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
